__d(function(g,r,i,a,m,e,d){Object.defineProperty(e,"__esModule",{value:!0}),e.default=void 0;var n={t_and_c:"Terms and conditions of use\n\n\n1. Before you register, ensure to have a valid email id and a phone number.\n\n2. In case user wants to change the mobile no. and email id, it can do so by registering new mobile no. and email id and cancel the existing registered no. and id.\n\n3. The mobile application is prohibited to limited usage.\n\n4. The company can terminate any mobile application user if found misleading and contrary to the policies of the Company without any further intimation to the user.\n\n5. The payment clauses solely depend on the Company purview.\n\n6. This mobile application does not create any right in favour of any of the application users.\n\n7. All taxes existing or new levied by the Govt. will be payable extra by the applicant, without disputing the same.\n\n8. The company reserves all the right to withdraw the application anytime without any references.\n\n9. Any disputes are within the jurisdiction of the Kolkata Court.",p_p:"The Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act was passed in early August of 2023. The act is expected to come into force to companies like us anytime through a government notification.\n\n \n\nDue to this \u2018Personal Data\u2019 of any individual (employee, dealer, customer, business partner) is extreme critical and sensitive entity of any organisation and we need to take outmost protection and privacy of such \u2018data\u2019 and this is to be informed via our \u2018 Privacy Policy\u2019 to whosever who visits to our websites.\n Please note any violation in particular for the failure to implement information security measures necessary to mitigate the risk of a personal data breach - could result in fines of up to 250 crore INR/$30 million.\n\n \n\nIn connection to the above in our recent revamped website, I found some changes is needed and my drafted Privacy Policy is attached for your reference.\n\n \n\nAlso, I found my name and mobile number is visible in the policy, mentioned as \u2018Grievance Officer (as per requirement of Information Technology Rules)\u2019 without my knowledge and consent. Nowhere any person name/contact details should be written, and instead of only email id and contact number should be displayed. You may give email / contact no for our Legal Officer, who can connect us (IT Dept.) later any IT related issues.\n\n \n\nYou can enquire/check with other websites or related website design vendor.",r_p:"Refund Policy\n\n    \n1. Star Cement Limited (SCL) will not be responsible for any refunds arising out of any failures in online payments and in case the amount gets deducted from customers saving/current account, credit/debit card and does not get credited in SCL account, before the transaction is complete. Users in this case will have to contact his Bank to clarify the same and get refund.\n    \n2. SCL shall have right to adjust any excess amount paid by the party with the future orders or else with the final settlement whichever so is earlier.\n    \n3. SCL shall have the right to forfeit or adjust the whole or part of customers security deposit held with SCL in the manner as SCL may deem fit at the time of final settlement account.\n    \n4. SCL reserves the right to modify and amend refund policy at its sole discretion."};e.default=n},1394,[]);
